      "nets": ["unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "The STM32L476 VBAT pin is explicitly unconnected, while the design has no separate battery supply.",
      "expected": "If no backup battery is used, standard STM32 practice is to connect VBAT to VDD so the backup domain has a defined supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"65\") (name \"unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere in the three `.kicad_sch` files or `PCB.net`/`PCB.cir`"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU's backup domain, including RTC and backup registers, may not be powered or usable. The main MCU functions may still operate, but this leaves the backup supply pin without the expected defined connection.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "U2's VBAT pin is left unconnected despite the design having no backup battery. Connecting it to VDD is standard practice when no battery is used; the likely effect is loss or unreliable operation of the MCU backup domain."
}

